WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.800
- All right, we always like to wrap things

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.330
up with something fun and uplifting.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.530
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.266
(upbeat music sting)

00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:07.230
(crowd cheering)

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.790
Y'all know how much I appreciate

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:11.400
and love my musical
director, Jason Halbert.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.840
I'm so happy to have him in my corner.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:13.890
I would have no career without him,

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.470
but I'm not the only person
that he has encouraged

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.360
over the years, there's many of us.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.640
In fact, he's been supporting
an author in Nashville

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.740
and she's just published her first book

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.600
called "In The Shadow Garden",

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.640
let's say hi to Liz Parker everybody.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.685
(crowd cheering)

00:00:29.685 --> 00:00:31.368
Hi, Liz.

00:00:31.368 --> 00:00:32.201
What's up?

00:00:32.201 --> 00:00:33.090
So it's great to see you.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.830
So congrats on the book.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.155
- Thank you so much.
You're holding it, it's-

00:00:38.155 --> 00:00:39.990
(Kelly laughing)
Thank you.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.940
- I know, it's cool when
it's, like, tangible, right?

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.770
And you do something and it
comes out and, like, people-

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.450
it's so cool. Yeah, that's a cool place.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.820
So you say that Jason was pivotal, right,

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.350
in pushing you to do this?

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.230
- Yeah, so I've been
writing for, like, 12 years.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.580
This is my first published book,

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.020
but it's my sixth book

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.673
and Jason actually read my
second book and liked it,

00:00:59.673 --> 00:01:00.506
(Liz and crowd laughing)

00:01:00.506 --> 00:01:03.630
and provided feedback and
he and his entire family

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.760
have been so supportive of my writing

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.310
and so enthusiastic ever since.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.620
And that kind of support is, just,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.270
it keeps you going when you're trying

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.580
to break into an industry like publishing.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.110
- [Kelly] Absolutely.
- I'm so grateful.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.790
- Yeah, and the cool thing about Jason is,

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.830
he is, like, super honest,
like he's supportive

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.630
but he is encouraging and, like, honest.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.220
And that's good, though.
You need those people.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.770
That's why he's helped
me my entire career.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.570
But can you tell us more about the book?

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.510
- Yeah, so, people tell
you to write what you know,

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:34.337
and I know a lot about
trauma and gardening,

00:01:34.337 --> 00:01:35.170
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.170
and so I thought what
if something beautiful

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.550
could grow from our pain?

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.440
And that became "In The Shadow Garden".

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.820
So it's like kind of in
the vein of practical magic

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.590
where it's witchy but it's not scary,

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:49.890
and it follows three
generations of empathic witches

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.200
who can heal their neighbor's pain,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.670
and they bury it in their garden.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.050
And then there's like a rival family

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:58.560
that has magical bourbon that
lets you forget a memory.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.130
So it asks the question "is
it better to heal over time

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:05.070
or to forget what caused you pain?".

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.440
And I'm just so excited to see it, like,

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.700
in bookstores and on
bookshelves as a real book.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.550
- Yeah, I'm, I'm excited.
I wanna see the movie.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:15.960
That's what I, I mean I like the book.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.610
I- your Mind doesn't have a budget,

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.760
but that would make a great
movie, is all I'm saying.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.864
Oh, there is a movie?

00:02:21.864 --> 00:02:23.763
(Liz laughing)

00:02:23.763 --> 00:02:26.850
- So a really great
film production company

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:29.820
actually read the book and
fell in love with the book,

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.800
and before it was even published

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.080
they optioned the rights
for film and series.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.033
- What?!
(crowd cheering)

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.451
- [Liz] On the screen someday.

00:02:37.451 --> 00:02:41.910
- This is incredible, that's
incredible. Congratulations.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.140
I know I was listening
to you tell the story

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.160
and I was like "well, I
can't wait to read the book,

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.020
but I also wanna see it".

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.424
Thanks Liz, and congratulations
again. This is incredible.

00:02:49.424 --> 00:02:50.520
(crowd cheering)

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.008
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:53.008 --> 00:02:53.841
(ding)

00:02:53.841 --> 00:02:55.619
And at this point, we
usually give our guest

00:02:55.619 --> 00:02:58.530
a check for $1,000 from
our season-long partner

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.810
Pilot Pen, makers of G2, the go-to pen

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:01.770
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.830
But today, Liz wants to
help someone in the audience

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.800
pursue their passions with
a little unexpected cash.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.400
So one of you has $1,000
check securely taped

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.193
beneath your chairs, so look.

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:14.970
(crowd cheering)
(drumroll)

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.980
Y'all aren't looking hard enough.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.136
Are y'all like this at Christmas?

00:03:19.136 --> 00:03:20.420
(upbeat music sting)

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.170
(crowd cheering)

00:03:25.681 --> 00:03:28.431
Yeah! (laughing)

00:03:30.584 --> 00:03:33.090
What's your name? Where are you from?

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.380
- Hi, I'm Ashley Hart.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.810
I'm originally from Texas,
but I live in Los Angeles now

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:37.920
for about a year.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.900
- There's some Texas here
today, y'all representing,

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.130
I like this audience.

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:42.810
Well, how will you use the money?

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:45.030
- I'm in law school. Don't cry.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.680
And, so it's very expensive and it's-

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.390
I come from a low-income family,

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:49.830
so this is just like
a really big blessing.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.012
Thank you so much.

00:03:51.012 --> 00:03:51.968
(crowd cheering)

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:54.930
- Wow. Well, you know what?

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:57.690
That is really amazing and I, I feel like,

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:59.580
opportunity like that should
not be taken from anyone,

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.260
so I'm gonna give you five grand, too,

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.002
to help you, for law school.

00:04:03.002 --> 00:04:03.835
(crowd cheering)

00:04:03.835 --> 00:04:05.160
- Thank you.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:08.640
- That's really incredible.
You gotta keep going at it.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.140
Don't let the money thing stop you.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.610
Keep going for it, all right?

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:12.660
- Thank you so much.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.210
- Yeah, gotta help my Texas girl out.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.550
All right, well thank you so
much to all our guests today,

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:21.600
Eddie Redmayne, Emily
Deschanel, Dara Yu, John Indigo,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:22.433
Y'all have a great day,

00:04:22.433 --> 00:04:24.240
and if it's not, try and change it.

